FEX: a shared mapping made writable drops the translations of its mirrors (SteamARM)

SMC tracking (mtrack) write-protects every writable view of shared memory
whose code FEX translated through another view (MarkGuestExecutableRange).
A guest mprotect that makes such a view writable again lifts that
protection on the host, and FEX only invalidated translations in the
mprotected range itself, where there are none: later writes through the
view rewrote code whose translations FEX kept running. ART's JIT code
cache is exactly that: a memfd mapped as an executable view and a writable
view, and ScopedCodeCacheWrite flips the writable view from read-only to
read-write around every code write. After code cache collections reused
memory, x86-64 ART under FEX ran old methods' code and computed wrong
results, 3 runs of 3 (MEASURED; correct with FEX_SMCCHECKS=full;
SteamARM benchmarks/stage25-art-x86-fex.txt, tests/android/run.sh). Now the
mirrors' translations of the range are invalidated when a shared mapping
becomes writable; running that code again translates it and protects the
view again. Nothing changes for private memory or with other SMC modes.

diff --git a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SyscallsSMCTracking.cpp b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SyscallsSMCTracking.cpp
--- a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SyscallsSMCTracking.cpp
+++ b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SyscallsSMCTracking.cpp
@@ -541,6 +541,7 @@
 
 uint64_t SyscallHandler::GuestMprotect(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState* Thread, void* addr, size_t len, int prot) {
   uint64_t Result {};
+  fextl::vector<std::pair<uint64_t, uint64_t>> MirrorRanges;
 
   {
     auto lk = FEXCore::GuardSignalDeferringSection(VMATracking.Mutex, Thread);
@@ -559,9 +560,48 @@
     }
 
     TrackMprotect(Thread, addr, len, prot);
+
+    // Shared memory made writable: the host mprotect just lifted the write
+    // protection SMC tracking had put on this view of memory whose code was
+    // translated through another view of it (MarkGuestExecutableRange
+    // protects every writable mirror), so its next rewrites would go unseen.
+    // Drop the translations of every view of the range now; running that code
+    // again translates it again and protects this view again. ART's JIT
+    // flips the writable view of its code cache (a memfd mapped twice) from
+    // read-only to read-write around every code write (ScopedCodeCacheWrite),
+    // and x86-64 ART ran stale translations of freed methods after code cache
+    // collections (MEASURED, SteamARM benchmarks/stage25-art-x86-fex.txt).
+    if ((prot & PROT_WRITE) && SMCChecks == FEXCore::Config::CONFIG_SMC_MTRACK) {
+      const auto Base = reinterpret_cast<uint64_t>(addr);
+      const auto Top = Base + FEXCore::AlignUp(len, FEXCore::Utils::FEX_PAGE_SIZE);
+      auto Mapping = VMATracking.VMAs.lower_bound(Top);
+      while (Mapping != VMATracking.VMAs.begin()) {
+        --Mapping;
+        const auto MapBase = Mapping->first;
+        const auto MapTop = MapBase + Mapping->second.Length;
+        if (MapTop <= Base) {
+          break;
+        }
+        if (!Mapping->second.Flags.Shared || !Mapping->second.Resource) {
+          continue;
+        }
+        const auto OffsetBase = std::max(MapBase, Base) - MapBase + Mapping->second.Offset;
+        const auto OffsetTop = std::min(MapTop, Top) - MapBase + Mapping->second.Offset;
+        for (auto VMA = Mapping->second.Resource->FirstVMA; VMA; VMA = VMA->ResourceNextVMA) {
+          const auto Lo = std::max<uint64_t>(VMA->Offset, OffsetBase);
+          const auto Hi = std::min<uint64_t>(VMA->Offset + VMA->Length, OffsetTop);
+          if (Lo < Hi && VMA->Base != MapBase) {
+            MirrorRanges.emplace_back(Lo - VMA->Offset + VMA->Base, Hi - Lo);
+          }
+        }
+      }
+    }
   }
 
   InvalidateCodeRangeIfNecessary(Thread, reinterpret_cast<uint64_t>(addr), len, false);
+  for (const auto& [MirrorBase, MirrorLength] : MirrorRanges) {
+    TM.InvalidateGuestCodeRange(Thread, MirrorBase, MirrorLength);
+  }
 
   // Prepare for delayed code cache load after ld/Wine is done applying relocations.
   // Hooking into mprotect is a reliable heuristic that matches behavior of ld (for ELF) and Wine (for PE).
